=== TITLE: USG Breast (Bilateral) - Normal ===
=== IMPRESSION ===
NORMAL HIGH-RESOLUTION BILATERAL BREAST ULTRASOUND STUDY (ACR BI-RADS CATEGORY 1).
- No solid or cystic focal mass lesion.
- No architectural distortion, skin thickening, or axillary lymphadenopathy.

=== FINDINGS ===
STUDY: HIGH-RESOLUTION ULTRASONOGRAPHY OF BILATERAL BREASTS AND AXILLAE

OBSERVATIONS:
- RIGHT BREAST: Normal skin and subcutaneous fat. Fibroglandular parenchyma shows normal architecture and uniform echogenicity without focal solid mass, cyst, microcalcification, or ductal dilatation.
- LEFT BREAST: Normal skin, subcutaneous tissue, and fibroglandular parenchyma. No discrete nodule, mass lesion, or architectural distortion seen.
- RETROMAMMARY SPACES: Clear bilaterally. Cooper's ligaments intact.
- AXILLARY REGIONS: Bilateral axillae show no suspicious, enlarged, or matted lymphadenopathy. Normal fatty hila preserved.